    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's hollow. and the worst part is that i can't pretend anymore. i can't go back to the lab and pretend that every incremental discovery is part of some greater tapestry. it's just entropy. everything eventually just fades into nothing. i find myself wondering why anyone bothers to fight it. why struggle to stay in the dark when the dark is the only thing that's actually real?",
